{"id":"ec489e7282b59449","group":"58","path":"58/batch14/58-df-independent.md","title":"Independence","display":"df-independent — Independence","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-independent","aliases":["58-df-independent","Independence"],"display":"df-independent — Independence","depends_on":["[[../batch08/58-df-theory.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]","[[../batch13/58-df-consistency.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-independent"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-independent</span><span>Independence</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-independent — Independence"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"90ce6acf0c65af45\" href=\"?note=90ce6acf0c65af45\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-theory.md\">../batch08/58-df-theory.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"6996aaff4caeacce\" href=\"?note=6996aaff4caeacce\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-consistency.md\">../batch13/58-df-consistency.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T,\\Sigma,\\varphi,\\mathcal P,\\bot\\in V\">\\(T,\\Sigma,\\varphi,\\mathcal P,\\bot\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak C=\\langle\\Sigma,\\mathcal P,\\bot\\rangle\">\\(\\mathfrak C=\\langle\\Sigma,\\mathcal P,\\bot\\rangle\\)</span> is the designated proof context.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Theory}\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{Theory}\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\subseteq V\">\\(\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\subseteq V\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"90ce6acf0c65af45\" href=\"?note=90ce6acf0c65af45\" title=\"../batch08/58-df-theory.md\">../batch08/58-df-theory.md</a>, <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ConsistentTheory}_S\\subseteq V^4\">\\(\\mathrm{ConsistentTheory}_S\\subseteq V^4\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"6996aaff4caeacce\" href=\"?note=6996aaff4caeacce\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-consistency.md\">../batch13/58-df-consistency.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Independent}_S\\subseteq V^5\">\\(\\mathrm{Independent}_S\\subseteq V^5\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ind}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{Ind}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}independent} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{Independent}_S(T,\\varphi,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot) \\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Theory}(T,\\Sigma)\\land\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\land\n\\mathrm{ConsistentTheory}_S(T,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\land\n\\mathrm{ConsistentTheory}_S(T\\cup\\{\\varphi\\},\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\land\n\\mathrm{ConsistentTheory}_S(T\\cup\\{\\neg\\varphi\\},\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}independent} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{Independent}_S(T,\\varphi,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot) \\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Theory}(T,\\Sigma)\\land\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\land\n\\mathrm{ConsistentTheory}_S(T,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\land\n\\mathrm{ConsistentTheory}_S(T\\cup\\{\\varphi\\},\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\land\n\\mathrm{ConsistentTheory}_S(T\\cup\\{\\neg\\varphi\\},\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}independent\\text{-}context} \\vdash\n\\mathfrak C=\\langle\\Sigma,\\mathcal P,\\bot\\rangle\\to\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{Ind}_S(T,\\varphi)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Independent}_S(T,\\varphi,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}independent\\text{-}context} \\vdash\n\\mathfrak C=\\langle\\Sigma,\\mathcal P,\\bot\\rangle\\to\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{Ind}_S(T,\\varphi)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Independent}_S(T,\\varphi,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Statement <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi\">\\(\\varphi\\)</span> is independent of theory <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span> if neither <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T \\vdash \\varphi\">\\(T \\vdash \\varphi\\)</span> nor <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T \\vdash \\neg\\varphi\">\\(T \\vdash \\neg\\varphi\\)</span></li>\n<li>Equivalent: both <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T + \\varphi\">\\(T + \\varphi\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T + \\neg\\varphi\">\\(T + \\neg\\varphi\\)</span> are consistent</li>\n<li>The portable predicate carries the proof system, language, and contradiction formula explicitly; the binary notation is only a designated-context alias.</li>\n<li>ZFC cannot prove independence of CH from ZFC without additional axioms</li>\n<li>Forcing and inner models are primary tools for establishing independence</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Kunen, Set Theory, Chapter VIII</li>\n<li>Jech, Set Theory, Chapter 15</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch08/58-df-theory.md","status":"resolved","id":"90ce6acf0c65af45","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch08/58-df-theory.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-formula.md","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-consistency.md","status":"resolved","id":"6996aaff4caeacce","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-consistency.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch08/58-df-theory.md","status":"resolved","id":"90ce6acf0c65af45","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Theory}\\subseteq V^2$ and $\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\subseteq V$ (see [[../batch08/58-df-theory.md]], [[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]).","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-formula.md","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Theory}\\subseteq V^2$ and $\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\subseteq V$ (see [[../batch08/58-df-theory.md]], [[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]).","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-consistency.md","status":"resolved","id":"6996aaff4caeacce","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{ConsistentTheory}_S\\subseteq V^4$ (see [[../batch13/58-df-consistency.md]]).","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"T,\\Sigma,\\varphi,\\mathcal P,\\bot\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathfrak C=\\langle\\Sigma,\\mathcal P,\\bot\\rangle","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Theory}\\subseteq V^2","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\subseteq V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ConsistentTheory}_S\\subseteq V^4","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Independent}_S\\subseteq V^5","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Ind}_S\\subseteq V^2","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}independent} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{Independent}_S(T,\\varphi,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot) \\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Theory}(T,\\Sigma)\\land\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\Sigma)\\land\n\\mathrm{ConsistentTheory}_S(T,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\land\n\\mathrm{ConsistentTheory}_S(T\\cup\\{\\varphi\\},\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\land\n\\mathrm{ConsistentTheory}_S(T\\cup\\{\\neg\\varphi\\},\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}independent\\text{-}context} \\vdash\n\\mathfrak C=\\langle\\Sigma,\\mathcal P,\\bot\\rangle\\to\n\\bigl(\\mathrm{Ind}_S(T,\\varphi)\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Independent}_S(T,\\varphi,\\mathcal P,\\Sigma,\\bot)\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\varphi","display":false},{"tex":"T","display":false},{"tex":"T \\vdash \\varphi","display":false},{"tex":"T \\vdash \\neg\\varphi","display":false},{"tex":"T + \\varphi","display":false},{"tex":"T + \\neg\\varphi","display":false}],"bytes":1997,"backlinks":[{"id":"a11585cba9c21cfd","anchor":"ref-173","locations":["正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"[[58-df-independent]]"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-666","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch14/58-df-independent.md|58-df-independent]]（batch14）"}],"outgoing":["90ce6acf0c65af45","65418b505fc53093","6996aaff4caeacce"]}